# =============================================================================
# Second Brain — .gitignore
#
# Rule of thumb: ignore only what is (a) specific to ONE machine, (b) rewritten
# constantly by Obsidian, or (c) not yours to publish. Your NOTES (everything
# outside .obsidian) are always tracked and identical across devices.
#
# .obsidian/ — the ENTIRE folder is per-device by default: theme, appearance,
# which plugins are installed & enabled, hotkeys, app prefs, installed
# community themes (themes/), snippets, all of it. That means two devices can
# run completely different Obsidian setups off the same repo with zero risk
# of one device's config overwriting the other's on pull/push.
#
# EXCEPTIONS: .obsidian/plugins/obsidian-spaced-repetition/data.json stays
# tracked, so flashcard due dates still follow you between devices, and
# .obsidian/themes/Soft Paper/ stays tracked so the customized rainbow-folder
# theme itself is backed up on GitHub. See the "Exception" blocks below for
# how each carve-out works.
#
# The individual ignore lines below are commented out on purpose — the
# blanket ".obsidian/" line already covers every one of them, so they do
# nothing as-is. They're kept as a reference/toggle: if you ever want to go
# back to a narrower, per-file ignore instead of ignoring the whole folder,
# delete the blanket ".obsidian/" line and uncomment whichever of these you
# still want ignored.
#
# .obsidian/workspace.json
# .obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
# .obsidian/appearance.json
# .obsidian/community-plugins.json
# .obsidian/core-plugins.json
# .obsidian/app.json
# .obsidian/hotkeys.json
# .obsidian/themes/            (Soft Paper/ is tracked as an exception, below)
# .obsidian/daily-notes.json
# .obsidian/templates.json
# .obsidian/cache
# .obsidian/*.cache
# .obsidian/plugins/obsidian-excalidraw-plugin/*.local
# =============================================================================

.obsidian/

# --- Exceptions: un-ignore .obsidian/ itself first --------------------------
# Un-ignoring a file inside an ignored folder requires un-ignoring EVERY
# parent directory in its path, starting from .obsidian/ itself (the blanket
# rule above excludes that top-level folder too, not just its contents) —
# git won't look inside a directory it has already excluded. This one line
# pair is shared by both exception chains below; each chain then re-excludes
# and re-includes one level deeper.
!.obsidian/
.obsidian/*

# --- Exception: keep Spaced Repetition data syncing across devices ---------
!.obsidian/plugins/
.obsidian/plugins/*
!.obsidian/plugins/obsidian-spaced-repetition/
.obsidian/plugins/obsidian-spaced-repetition/*
!.obsidian/plugins/obsidian-spaced-repetition/data.json
#
# To track another plugin's data.json too (e.g. QuickAdd, Templater), add the
# same three-line chain for it:
#   !.obsidian/plugins/<plugin-folder-name>/
#   .obsidian/plugins/<plugin-folder-name>/*
#   !.obsidian/plugins/<plugin-folder-name>/data.json
# Then: git add -f .obsidian/plugins/<plugin-folder-name>/data.json

# --- Exception: back up the customized Soft Paper theme -------------------
# Same un-ignore chain as above, one level shorter since .obsidian/themes/
# only needs one intermediate directory un-ignored, not two.
!.obsidian/themes/
.obsidian/themes/*
!.obsidian/themes/Soft Paper/
.obsidian/themes/Soft Paper/*
!.obsidian/themes/Soft Paper/theme.css
!.obsidian/themes/Soft Paper/manifest.json
#
# To track another installed theme's folder too, add the same chain:
#   !.obsidian/themes/<Theme Name>/
#   .obsidian/themes/<Theme Name>/*
#   !.obsidian/themes/<Theme Name>/theme.css
#   !.obsidian/themes/<Theme Name>/manifest.json
# Then: git add -f ".obsidian/themes/<Theme Name>/theme.css" ".obsidian/themes/<Theme Name>/manifest.json"

# --- Obsidian's own trash ---------------------------------------------------
# Created when "Deleted files → Move to Obsidian trash" is enabled. A local undo
# buffer, not history. (07_Archive/ is your real archive — that IS tracked.)
.trash/

# --- Excalidraw -------------------------------------------------------------
# Your drawings (.excalidraw.md) are content and stay tracked — they live
# outside .obsidian/ so the blanket rule above doesn't touch them.
Excalidraw/*.compressed.md

# --- OS junk ----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# --- Editor / temp ----------------------------------------------------------
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.tmp

# =============================================================================
# OPTIONAL — uncomment if they apply to you
# =============================================================================

# Large binary attachments — if the vault gets heavy, or you'd rather not push
# screenshots and PDFs. Note: notes will then have broken embeds on a fresh clone.
# 08_Meta/Attachments/

# Private folders you don't want on a remote, even a private one.
# 01_Journal/
# 06_People/

# --- Work Style ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Tool dependencies and the pinned Dataview bundle the checker downloads.
tools/node_modules/
tools/.cache/

# Bookkeeping file written by `node tools/demo.cjs install`. Never commit it, and
# run `node tools/demo.cjs remove` before committing so sample data stays out of
# your real history.
.work-style-demo.json

# Proof screenshots can contain company information. Ignored by default so they
# never reach a remote by accident; delete this line if you want them tracked
# (and check your employer's rules first).
08_Meta/Attachments/Proofs/*
!08_Meta/Attachments/Proofs/_About Proofs.md
